{"id": 174, "result": [{"value": {"choices": []}, "id": "E30g_9Z3pk", "from_name": "flags", "to_name": "image", "type": "choices", "origin": "prediction"}, {"value": {"choices": ["No Error"]}, "id": "h_PmGas2cx", "from_name": "severity", "to_name": "gpt-output", "type": "choices", "origin": "prediction-changed"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0, "y": 0, "width": 64.2, "height": 18.4, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_1", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0, "y": 0, "width": 64.2, "height": 18.4, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_1", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0, "y": 0, "width": 64.2, "height": 18.4, "rotation": 0, "text": ["generation of new organelles, and control the general function of a cell. Built in to cell division are three checkpoints. In eukaryotic cells, these checkpoints are points within cell division in which the cell can go one of three ways: cell division can be halted either temporarily or permanently; cell division can proceed; or cell death can be triggered. These checkpoints have been evolutionarily conserved, meaning the checkpoint mechanisms in fruit flies are very similar to those in our own bodies. At each of the three checkpoints the cell determines whether or not all of the components and conditions have been met for cell division to proceed. Each checkpoint involves numerous molecules interacting in a set of complex cell signaling pathways. A change to these signaling pathways can cause cell division by promoting molecules to be expressed more than usual or by hindering molecules expression. Any of these changes in a normal cell\u2019s signaling pathways can cause the cell to replicate out of control\u2014this is cancer."]}, "id": "BB_1", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0.3, "y": 19.3, "width": 62.3, "height": 4.1, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_2", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0.3, "y": 19.3, "width": 62.3, "height": 4.1, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_2", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0.3, "y": 19.3, "width": 62.3, "height": 4.1, "rotation": 0, "text": ["The cell damage can be from an infection by certain viruses, from a physical source such as UV damage, from a chemical source such as benzene, or by a genetic defect that occurred during the rapid replication of fetal development."]}, "id": "BB_2", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0, "y": 24.1, "width": 62.9, "height": 10.2, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_3", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0, "y": 24.1, "width": 62.9, "height": 10.2, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_3", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0, "y": 24.1, "width": 62.9, "height": 10.2, "rotation": 0, "text": ["Once the cell is off track, multiple mutations begin to build up, including aneuploidy and structural errors. Aneuploidy means that a cell has an abnormal number of chromosomes. Structural errors occur when part of a chromosome is missing or not in its correct position. Pathologists and geneticists stain and view a cell\u2019s metaphase chromosomes using a light microscope. The stain used to help visualize the chromosomes causes a very specific banding pattern on the chromosome. Any structural changes or additional chromosomes are easily seen using this technique called karyotyping."]}, "id": "BB_3", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0, "y": 35.1, "width": 35.5, "height": 21.9, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_4", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0, "y": 35.1, "width": 35.5, "height": 21.9, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_4", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0, "y": 35.1, "width": 35.5, "height": 21.9, "rotation": 0, "text": ["A typical cell will have 46 chromosomes; any more or less is aneuploidy. If there is a large structural change or error in the chromosome, the banding pattern is altered. There are four types of structural errors\u2014translocations, inversions, deletions, and duplications (see Figure 1). Translocations arise when part of one chromosome breaks off and attaches to another chromosome. Inversions involve a section of a chromosome breaking off and then reattaching to the same chromosome upside down. A deletion is when a section of a chromosome is completely absent. Duplications occur when a section of the chromosome is repeated."]}, "id": "BB_4", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0, "y": 58, "width": 34.5, "height": 7.9, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_5", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0, "y": 58, "width": 34.5, "height": 7.9, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_5", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0, "y": 58, "width": 34.5, "height": 7.9, "rotation": 0, "text": ["An example of a virus that causes cancer is a subtype of the human papillomavirus (HPV) known as HPV-18. HPV-18 is particularly aggressive. Within the virus\u2019s 8,000 base pair DNA genome is the code for two checkpoint interfering proteins. Like many viruses,"]}, "id": "BB_5", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 37.2, "y": 35.600000000000016, "width": 26.943771067855277, "height": 25.860190806591405, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_6", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction-changed"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 37.2, "y": 35.600000000000016, "width": 26.943771067855277, "height": 25.860190806591405, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["image"]}, "id": "BB_6", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction-changed"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 37.2, "y": 35.600000000000016, "width": 26.943771067855277, "height": 25.860190806591405, "rotation": 0, "text": [""]}, "id": "BB_6", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction-changed"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0, "y": 65.9, "width": 63.6, "height": 12, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_7", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0, "y": 65.9, "width": 63.6, "height": 12, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_7", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 0, "y": 65.9, "width": 63.6, "height": 12, "rotation": 0, "text": ["HPV inserts itself into the chromosome of the host cell and the viral proteins are transcribed along with the host proteins. One of the two viral proteins targets a cell division repressor molecule. The first viral protein tags the repressor molecule for destruction by the cell. The second viral protein acts by binding to a host protein, which traps it. This particular host protein is a cell division promoter. By residing in the promoter\u2019s inhibition location, the virus causes the cell to move through the checkpoint and into cell division where a normal cell would have halted for repair before proceeding."]}, "id": "BB_7", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 47.445927700932565, "y": 61.49176062445794, "width": 5.987070931053907, "height": 2.6886383347788296, "rotation": 0}, "id": "vq3CsYet6J", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "manual"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 47.445927700932565, "y": 61.49176062445794, "width": 5.987070931053907, "height": 2.6886383347788296, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "vq3CsYet6J", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "manual"}, {"original_width": 970, "original_height": 720, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 47.445927700932